id: pm-nroemi
title: "A settings read of a missing settings.json carries no snapshot, so a later write replaces a file another process created meanwhile (a first-run telemetry opt-out can be lost)"
description: "readSettings on a missing settings.json returns cloned defaults with no persist-source snapshot, and writeSettings treats such settings as caller-constructed: it replaces the whole document without reconciling against what is on disk. A successful read of an existing, valid settings.json carries a snapshot, and its write reconciles leaf by leaf under the settings lock, so a concurrent edit to an untouched leaf survives and a conflicting one refuses. Fallback reads (unreadable, malformed or schema-invalid files) carry none either; they take the separate fallback write path. Reproduced on 2026.11.4 dist with a sandbox root: read A of the missing file, writer B records telemetry.enabled=false with first_run_prompt_completed=true, then A writes enabled=true and the stored file says enabled=true; the opt-out is lost. The same sequence over an existing file keeps enabled=false. Both consent writers that prompt and then write are affected on a fresh install: the runtime first-use prompt in core/telemetry/consent.ts and the pm init wizard in sdk/init.ts. The init wizard narrows the window by re-reading consent after its prompt (PR 1661 review), but the read-to-lock gap still clobbers when the file did not exist at that read. Found while answering a CodeRabbit finding on PR 1661 for the closed pm-gh1660; it is the missing-file residual of the closed lock-free settings family pm-bgcu."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: concurrency,configuration,settings,telemetry
created_at: "2026-11-04T18:35:24.672Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T21:13:51.020Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A missing-file settings read carries a snapshot (or equivalent marker) so writeSettings reconciles against the document present under the lock; a spec reproduces the read-missing, concurrent-create, stale-write sequence and shows the concurrent telemetry opt-out survives; a first write to a still-missing file behaves exactly as today; caller-constructed settings without a read keep their documented whole-document replacement"
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "A write from settings read while settings.json was missing reconciles against an empty stored document when the file has appeared, so a concurrent writer's leaves survive or the write refuses as stale_settings_snapshot"
actual_result: The write replaces the concurrently created settings.json wholesale; a recorded telemetry opt-out flips back to enabled
