comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-04T19:11:08.569Z","harness:claude-code","Scope update from the same PR 1661 review round. The pm init wizard no longer depends on this item for consent: its write passes the new WriteSettingsOptions.skipIfStored compare-and-set, consulted under the settings lock, so a consent choice stored by another process, even in a file that did not exist at the re-read, is kept. Still open here: the runtime first-use prompt in core/telemetry/consent.ts still writes without that check, so it can replace a concurrently created profile; when pm init targets the global profile itself, its create write replaces a concurrently created file; and any missing-file read loses a concurrent writer's non-consent fields. The first is a one-line skipIfStored adoption plus a kept message; the general fix is the missing-file snapshot this item describes.\n"
body: ""
